.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-ATTACH" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-attach - Attach or detach an explicitly selected personal resource


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team attach <team> <preview|tunnel> <resource> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Attach one of your personal previews or tunnels to the team so team grants can refer to it,
or detach it with --active=false. Only previews and tunnels can be attached.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--active\fP[=true]
	attach resource; set false to detach

.PP
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for attach

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team attach acme preview blog --generation 9
  pb team attach acme preview blog --active=false --generation 10
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
